# 9 — Java exceptions. Klepton's JNI never has one pending, so a call that
# throws on Android (AssetManager.open of a missing asset, new ZipFile of a
# missing OBB) returns null with nothing to check, and the guest reads through
# it: a Scanner over null, strlen(NULL), a crash. Give each thread a pending
# throwable, the ExceptionCheck/Occurred/Clear/Throw/ThrowNew that read and set
# it, and raise it where Android would. Any Java call clears a stale one first
# (calling into Java with one pending is already illegal on Android).
python3 - "$K/runtime" <<'EOF'
